   "rule": "Don't raise a finding just to swap a correct approved translation for a synonym or an equally valid alternative wording. If the existing zh-TW text is accurate and natural, a suggestion that is only \"interchangeable\" with it is not a fix. Examples: 報表 and 報告 are interchangeable for a crash \"report\", so don't push one over the other. Different quantifiers for permission items are also interchangeable. In the same way, don't propose rewording a tracker-protection message when the result is no better than the approved text. This does not cover real defects. Still flag a translation that drops or changes the source meaning (for example, 'older than %S months' rendered as '%S months ago'), leaves English untranslated, or breaks the glossary.",
